description:
## Finding

uuencoding-multi and yencoding-multi are analogous multi-part reassembly crates but use different names for their error types:

- uuencoding-multi/src/error.rs: pub enum MultiUuError { EmptyCollection, DecodeError(UuError), DuplicatePart }
- yencoding-multi/src/error.rs: pub enum AssemblyError { OverlappingPart, OutOfRange, CrcMismatch, Incomplete, DataLengthMismatch, TotalSizeTooLarge, MalformedPartRange, InconsistentCrc }

## Impact

A caller writing a generic handler for both encoding formats needs to match on two separate error enum hierarchies with different names and completely disjoint variant sets. Neither type implements a shared trait. A function that wraps both in its own error type must box or map from two unrelated types. CrcMismatch exists in AssemblyError but has no analogue in MultiUuError (UU has no CRC). However, the structural mismatch goes beyond justified protocol differences — top-level names like EmptyCollection vs Incomplete for 'nothing to reassemble/missing data' describe overlapping conditions.
